# Agent assets sync (Cursor + Claude + Codex)

This repo mirrors agent-facing assets in three tool-specific trees. They must stay identical.

## Layout

| Asset | Cursor (canonical for skills) | Claude Code | Codex | Cursor Agents legacy |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Skills | `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` | `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` | — | `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` |
| Prompt briefs | `.cursor/prompts/*.md` | — | `.codex/prompts/*.md` | — |

Do **not** sync `.claude/settings.local.json`, `.claude/launch.json` or `.codex/config.toml` (local/tool-specific).

## When editing

1. Edit the file in **any** mirrored path for that asset type.
2. Run `npm run sync:agent-assets` if you need an immediate full reconcile.
3. The Cursor hook auto-propagates edits under those paths after each file write.

## Agent behavior

- Prefer `.cursor/skills/` and `.cursor/prompts/` when creating or updating assets in Cursor.
- After manual edits to mirrored files, run `npm run sync:agent-assets` before finishing the task.
- Never leave `.claude/skills`, `.agents/skills`, `.codex/prompts` or `.cursor/*` out of sync.
- Prompt briefs in `.cursor/prompts/` / `.codex/prompts/` are dev guidance; production runtime lives in `lib/whatsapp/*-agent.ts`.

## Quick commands

```bash
npm run sync:agent-assets
node scripts/sync-agent-assets.mjs --from .cursor/skills/whatsapp-agent/SKILL.md
```
